# qemu.devices / qemu.devices.intx (M1-09): the kernel's devtest (edu: MSI or
# INTx, a refused MSI move, DMA; virtio-net: RX moved to another CPU, ARP round
# trip), its block-layer test (M1-10) and the FAT32 mount of the virtio disk's
# EFI system partition ran during boot. A file read from /disk by a program
# sleeps until the disk's interrupt ends it (M1-10); then the interrupt counts.
diskread    /bin/cat /disk/hello.txt
interrupts  /bin/cat /proc/interrupts
